const content="<article data-editorial-version=\"3\" class=\"sn-page\"><div class=\"sn-read\"><a href=\"/supporters/\">← Featured sponsors</a><p class=\"sn-kicker\">Marine Diesel Engine · Sponsor feature</p><img class=\"sn-logo\" src=\"/images/supporters/water-makers-australia/logo.webp\" alt=\"Water Makers Australia logo\" width=\"210\" height=\"100\"><h1>Water Makers Australia: make fresh water offshore</h1><p class=\"sn-intro\">Water Makers Australia supplies marine reverse-osmosis systems that turn seawater into fresh water. For cruising owners, the product provides water for cooking, washing and showers with less dependence on a freshwater point ashore.</p><img class=\"sn-hero\" src=\"/images/supporters/water-makers-australia/small.webp\" alt=\"Water Makers Australia single-membrane system and its components\" width=\"1200\" height=\"1200\"><section><h2>Size production around the boat</h2><p>The company offers configurations rated up to 80, 160 and 240 litres per hour, depending on the membrane arrangement. Choosing a system involves the crew&#x27;s demand and the power available to operate it.</p><p>We like that the purchase can be considered as part of the boat&#x27;s working systems. Freshwater production is useful when it fits the way the vessel is run, not merely when a capacity figure looks impressive. Daily consumption and operating arrangements give the choice a practical basis.</p></section><section><h2>Modular parts and service access</h2><p>Pumps, filters and membranes can be installed separately. That allows the equipment to be arranged around spaces in an already fitted-out boat while considering how service items will be reached.</p><p>Standard parts and filter cartridges also support routine maintenance. For owners accustomed to looking after machinery, we appreciate an approach that considers access and replacement supplies as well as the initial installation.</p></section><section><h2>Why we feature the business</h2><p>Making fresh water at sea can make everyday cruising more comfortable and give owners greater flexibility about refill stops. That is the direct reason we feature Water Makers Australia.</p><p>The range offers different production capacities and a modular installation approach to help the capability fit different vessels. For an owner planning more time away, it is a practical system to assess alongside the other equipment that supports life aboard.</p></section><div class=\"sn-contact\"><a href=\"https://www.watermakers.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"sponsored nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Talk to Water Makers Australia ↗</a><a href=\"/supporters/\">More featured sponsors</a></div></div></article><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"Article\", \"headline\": \"Water Makers Australia: make fresh water offshore\", \"description\": \"Make fresh water offshore with Water Makers Australia, offering marine reverse-osmosis systems with different capacities and modular components.\", \"image\": \"https://marinedieselengine.com.au/images/supporters/water-makers-australia/small.webp\", \"author\": {\"@type\": \"Organization\", \"name\": \"Marine Diesel Engine\"}, \"dateModified\": \"2026-11-05\", \"mainEntityOfPage\": \"https://marinedieselengine.com.au/supporters/water-makers-australia/\"}</script>";
